{% tool-context
   title="Load Balancer Visualizer"
   question="What is load balancing?"
   definition="Load balancing routes each request to an eligible backend. A safe design must distribute work, eject unhealthy instances, preserve spare capacity, and prevent retries from multiplying an incident."
   inputs="Change traffic, routing policy, affinity, backend capacity and weight, health ejection, and caller retry behavior."
   outcome="Trace request distribution, saturation, queueing, health ejection, availability, tail latency, and the consequence users experience."
   experiment="Compare a node failure, slow instance, affinity hotspot, zone loss, retry storm, and gradual recovery. Find the policy that keeps failures isolated instead of moving pressure elsewhere." /%}

